@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Use it when you want raw text rather than rich formatting.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers or objects, does not word wrap or crop to the console width, and does not interpret markup or replace emoji codes. It does support highlighting (on by default, controlled by the ``highlight`` argument) and a basic ``style``. Here's an example::
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", "World", sep=" ")
+
+Output from ``out`` still goes through the normal print path, so render hooks, capturing, and file output all work as they do for print.
+
+
